    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "You think Zuckerberg lives on his salary? Here's why he doesn't need to.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 3.81,
        "window": 4.4,
        "fill": 0.866
      },
      {
        "scene": "promise",
        "text": "His base salary was $1, for a whole year of running one of the biggest companies on Earth. So where does the real money of the richest come from?",
        "start": 4.7,
        "seconds": 8.3,
        "window": 8.83,
        "fill": 0.94
      },
      {
        "scene": "coffee",
        "text": "A salary that won't even buy a coffee? So what do the richest live on?",
        "start": 13.53,
        "seconds": 3.61,
        "window": 4.03,
        "fill": 0.896
      },
      {
        "scene": "shares",
        "text": "For the richest, wealth isn't a paycheck. It's shares in their companies, which grow with them.",
        "start": 17.57,
        "seconds": 5.09,
        "window": 5.57,
        "fill": 0.914
      },
      {
        "scene": "untaxed",
        "text": "And in America, shares that rise aren't taxed as income until they're sold.",
        "start": 23.13,
        "seconds": 4.17,
        "window": 4.63,
        "fill": 0.901
      },
      {
        "scene": "jet",
        "text": "But if they don't sell, how do they pay for the jets and the houses?",
        "start": 27.77,
        "seconds": 3.12,
        "window": 3.57,
        "fill": 0.874
      },
      {
        "scene": "borrow",
        "text": "The richest can borrow against their shares. A loan isn't income, so there's no income tax.",
        "start": 31.33,
        "seconds": 5.58,
        "window": 6.2,
        "fill": 0.9
      },
      {
        "scene": "turn",
        "text": "Here's the twist. The 25 richest Americans grew $401B richer in 5 years, and paid $13.6B in federal income tax.",
        "start": 37.53,
        "seconds": 10.56,
        "window": 11.23,
        "fill": 0.94
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "That's why a paycheck barely matters to them. Shares grow untaxed until sold, loans aren't income, and for those richest Americans, the true tax rate was 3.4%.",
        "start": 48.77,
        "seconds": 10.92,
        "window": 11.43,
        "fill": 0.955
      },
      {
        "scene": "loop",
        "text": "And a paycheck is taxed every payday. So who pays the higher rate, you or them?",
        "start": 60.2,
        "seconds": 4.46,
        "window": 4.83,
        "fill": 0.923
      }
    ]
